se store only per s167-D1; legacy and console/supercharge declare the rung ABSENT); (c) the rung NAME '-graphic' remains a DECLARED DEFAULT, STILL UNRATIFIED - this ruling does not name it; (d) the dark-leg $note contrast dispute (3.66:1 vs 3.42:1 on #CC4333) is STILL an open residual, untouched. RETIREMENT, NEVER DELETION: #DA1A00 and #137F3C are retired AS GRAPHIC LEGS ONLY - they REMAIN THE RULED INK/TEXT VALUES elsewhere (rag/error-ink light and rag/success-ink light, s144-D1/s151-D1/s155-D1), which this ruling does NOT touch. #3F6FB5 is retired as a graphic leg outright (it was never an ink value). MEASURED FIRST-HAND AT THIS SITTING, not trusted from the export - WCAG 2.x relative-luminance ratio on #FFFFFF: #F3543E = 3.415:1, #C58900 = 3.021:1, #57A369 = 3.067:1, #6893D3 = 3.133:1. All four clear dv-016 (>=3:1); NONE of them is text-grade (all below 4.5) and none is claimed to be - the rung is a GRAPHIC rung and the ink rungs carry text. NOTE THE DIRECTION OF TRAVEL: the three changed legs move DOWN in contrast (5.086 -> 3.415, 5.086 -> 3.067, 5.057 -> 3.133) because the tuner's job was to normalise chroma and lift lightness; this is a DELIBERATE, EYE-RULED trade of text-grade headroom for chromatic strength on the graphic rung, and it is legal because dv-016 is the rung's governing threshold. MEASURED RESIDUAL, DECLARED NOT FIXED: the export's stated chroma reference ("normalise to C 0.1796") is NOT achieved by three of the four hexes - measured OKLCH chroma is red 0.1986, green 0.1151, blue 0.1071, amber 0.1404. Only the red is near the stated target; green and blue sit well under it, almost certainly because C 0.1796 at those hues and lightnesses is outside the sRGB gamut and the tuner clipped. HUE LOCK HOLDS within rounding (red 30.72->30.82, green 150.06->149.89, blue 257.85->258.13). THE HEXES ARE WHAT DAVE RULED AND THE HEXES ARE WHAT IS SEATED - the chroma-normalisation NARRATIVE is an unproven description of them, not a constraint they satisfy. Dave's to reopen if the description mattered.
